// Trithemius and the Secret Alphabets — an author and his books, and one
// cipher alphabet whose forms are pending.
//
// From the wing's research file trithemius.verified.json. Its fact-check could
// read the English Agrippa of 1651 (EEBO-TCP A26565) and the site's own house
// data, and relied for catalogue facts on the search-backed Theban check; much
// else in the file was recollection, and every point its fact-check left
// unresolved is either left out here or given with its uncertainty. The
// quotations from J.F.'s English were checked word for word against the TCP
// transcription. The letters are the cipher alphabet of the Golden Dawn's
// Cipher Manuscripts, which the sources call Trithemius's: no form of any of
// them was seen, the inventory and order are provisional, and every letter
// carries glyph: null until the signs are traced.
